# shadcn/ui Conventions

This project uses the **`new-york`** style with the **`zinc`** base colour and **`lucide`** icon library. Configuration lives in `components.json`.

## Vendored, not customised

Treat every file in `src/components/ui/*` as **vendored from the shadcn registry**:

- ❌ Do **not** restructure the file (rename exports, change component shape, etc.).
- ✅ You may apply small, surgical Tailwind class tweaks for the project's design language, but leave the API intact.
- ✅ Custom UI helpers belong **outside** `ui/` — e.g. `src/components/ui/comet-card.tsx` is OK because it's clearly project-specific, but new utility components should be placed in `src/components/` instead.

## CLI workflow

```bash
# Add a new primitive
npx shadcn@latest add <name>

# Re-sync local components against registry (overwrites!)
npx shadcn@latest add <name> --overwrite

# Check for upstream updates
npx shadcn@latest diff
```

Always run `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run build` after running the CLI.

## When asked to add a new primitive

1. Run `npx shadcn@latest add <name>` — this will install required Radix peers automatically.
2. Verify the new file ended up in `src/components/ui/`.
3. If the CLI asks about overrides for `tailwind.config`, choose the option that **does not** create one — Tailwind v4 in this project is CSS-only via `src/app/globals.css`.

## Forms

When using shadcn's `Form` primitive, pair with `react-hook-form` + `zod` (v3) + `@hookform/resolvers/zod`. See `src/app/(root)/contact/page.tsx` for the canonical pattern.

## Future migration to `new-york-v4`

The current style key is `new-york`. The newer `new-york-v4` style uses OKLCH tokens and `data-slot` attributes, which would also require migrating `src/app/globals.css` from HSL-based tokens. **Do not undertake this migration piecemeal** — it's an all-or-nothing change.
